<title>MALTA: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>MALTA GOVERNMENT LIST (961028)</p>
<p> *************************************************************</p>
<p> * 28 Oct 1996 - Labour leader Alfred Sant was sworn in as   *</p>
<p> *		   prime minister by President Ugo Mifsud	*</p>
<p> *		   Bonnici, after the Nationalist Party was    *</p>
<p> *		   defeated in general elections. Official     *</p>
<p> *		   results gave Labour 50.72 percent.	    *</p>
<p> *************************************************************</p>
<p>  President..............................Dr Ugo MIFSUD BONNICI</p>
<p>(Elected 4 April 94 for 5-year term)</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p>  Prime Minister.................................Alfred SANT**</p>
<p>    (Sworn in 28 Oct 96)			  (**See Note Above)</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p>OUTGOING NATIONALIST PARTY GOVERNMENT (Formed 27 Feb 1992):</p>
<p>  Prime Minister...........................Edward FENECH ADAMI</p>
<p>(Sworn in for new five-year term 25 Feb 1992)</p>
<p>  Deputy Prime Minister.........................Guido DE MARCO</p>
<p>(also Minister of Foreign Affairs)</p>
<p>				 - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p>  Economic Services.............................Joseph BONNICI</p>
<p>(Also Finance Secretary)</p>
<p>  Education &amp; Human Resources...................Michael FALZON</p>
<p>  Environment.........................Dr Francis ZAMMIT DIMECH</p>
<p>  Finance...........................................John DALLI</p>
<p>  Food, Agriculture &amp; Fisheries....................Censu GALEA</p>
<p>  Foreign Affairs................................See Deputy PM</p>
<p>  Gozo Island Affairs.............................Anton TABONE</p>
<p>  Internal Affairs..................................Tonio BORG</p>
<p>  Justice.......................................Michael REFALO</p>
<p>  Social Security &amp; Social Development.............Louis GALEA</p>
<p>  Transport, Communications &amp; Technology.....Dr Michael FRENDO</p>
<p>  Youth &amp; the Arts..............................Richard MUSCAT</p>
<p>				     - - - - - -</p>
<p>PARLIAMENTARY SECRETARIES:</p>
<p>  Economic Services.......................Joseph PSAILA SAVONA</p>
<p>  Education &amp; Human Resources....................Joseph CASSAR</p>
<p>  Environment......................................Ninu ZAMMIT</p>
<p>  Finance.......................See Economic Services Minister</p>
<p>  Internal &amp; Social Development...............John Rizzo NAUDI</p>
<p>				     - - - - - -</p>
<p>  Central Bank Governor.......................Francis VASSALLO</p>
<p>				     - - - - - -</p>
<p>	 NOTE: Any comments/queries on the content of this</p>
<p>		 government list, please contact the Reuter</p>
<p>		 Editorial Reference Unit, London, on (171) 542</p>
<p>		 7968.</p>
<p>			    (End Government List)</p>
</text>
